⚠️ One major issue: Excel macro security

This is probably the most important part of your setup.

Microsoft blocks VBA macros from files that are considered to come from the Internet, including files downloaded from SharePoint/OneDrive in some circumstances. Microsoft recommends approaches such as opening the file in the desktop app, using appropriate trusted-site policies, or managing the file's trust/security configuration. 

For a company automation, I would not simply disable Excel macro security globally.

Instead, your IT administrator can establish an appropriate trusted configuration for the organization's SharePoint environment. Microsoft also documents Trusted Locations for Office files, where files in those locations can have active content enabled. 


